{
  "name": "Spirits from Beyond",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "CcHjGNEV3n9NvyuJ",
  "img": "icons/magic/death/undead-ghosts-trio-blue.webp",
  "folder": "WAvLaXb3LGEGkvRL",
  "sort": 200000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can call forth spirits of the dead to empower you and your allies. When you take a Bonus Action to give a creature a Bardic Inspiration die, you can call on the power of a random spirit: roll the Bardic Inspiration die and check the Spirits from Beyond table. The spirit stays channeled until you unleash it or finish a Short or Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Controlled Channeling.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can expend a use of your Bardic Inspiration to channel a specific spirit of your choice instead of rolling. Its number must be no higher than the highest number of your Bardic Inspiration die; with a d8, for example, you can choose any spirit up to the Shade.</p><p><strong>Unleashing a Spirit.</strong> As a Magic action, you can unleash one of your channeled spirits at one creature you can see within 30 feet of you. The spirit then takes effect; if it calls for a saving throw, the DC equals your Bard spell save DC.</p><h4>Spirits from Beyond</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Bardic Insp. Die</th><th>Spirit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td><strong>Beloved.</strong> The target regains Hit Points equal to one roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Charisma modifier.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Sharpshooter.</strong> The target takes Force damage equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Charisma modifier.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><strong>Avenger.</strong> Until the end of your next turn, any creature that hits the target with a melee attack roll takes Force damage equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><strong>Renegade.</strong> The target can immediately take a Reaction to teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Fortune Teller.</strong> The target has Advantage on D20 Tests until the start of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><strong>Wayfarer.</strong> The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to a roll of your Bardic Inspiration die plus your Bard level, and while it has them, its Speed increases by 10 feet.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><strong>Trickster.</strong> The target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, it takes Psychic damage equal to two rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die and has the Charmed condition until the start of your next turn; on a success, it takes only half as much damage.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td><strong>Shade.</strong> The target has the Invisible condition until the end of its next turn, or until it makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell. When the invisibility ends, each creature in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take Necrotic damage equal to two rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><strong>Arsonist.</strong> The target makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking Fire damage equal to four rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die on a failure or half as much on a success.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><strong>Coward.</strong> The target and each creature of your choice in a 30-foot Emanation originating from it must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn. While Frightened this way, a creature's Speed is halved (round down), and it can take either an action or a Bonus Action, not both.</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td><strong>Brute.</strong> Each creature of your choice in a 30-foot Emanation originating from the target makes a Strength saving throw. On a failure, it takes Thunder damage equal to three rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die and has the Prone condition; on a success, it takes only half as much damage.</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td><strong>Priest.</strong> The target regains Hit Points equal to two rolls of your Bardic Inspiration die, and one of the following conditions of your choice ends on it: Blinded, Charmed, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, or Stunned.</td></tr></tbody></table><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-E6c71IWYMFojmuYd\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The activities of the main spirits use your Bardic Inspiration die (two rolls of it are its scale value doubled; reroll dice in the dialog if you want separate rolls). Apply the conditions (Charmed, Invisible, Frightened, Prone) yourself.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
